A||||2||riverpete||front end vibration
Z||000000||riverpete||07-11-99||05:05 PM||||I have an 87 Fiero G.T that has vibration in  the front when I get to about 55 to 75 miles  an hour.Seems to come from driver side.I had  stock rims on it and front driver side rim   was out of round so I have recently put new  rims and tires on it but still have  vibration problem.I am not a very good  mechanic and am looking for a shop in the    Riverside or San Bernardino,L.A. county area  that can find problem and fix it.If it is    something simple will attempt to fix problem  myself.I would also like to lower it,so I am  looking for a shop to do both.       
Z||000001||Cooter||07-11-99||05:11 PM||||Ball Joints, tie rod ends shocks, and steering dampner need to be checked. A bent or out of round wheel really causes a lot of wear on these parts which are not the greatest to begin with.
Z||000002||theogre||07-11-99||05:49 PM||||before doing anything else. have the wheel ballance, and inflation pressure, checked. also look for any uneven wear on the tread. those 3 things will tell you a huge ammount of information. (Fiero "sticker" inflation is 30 PSI front, 30 PSI rear. Personally I like them 3 PSI higher. even one soft tire can cause all sorts of odd handling problems. All tires should be within a 1 PSI window for most purposes in Fiero.)
